// YZC-0106: a self-recursive #(...) boc with a non-Unit return type, whose
// last statement is a value-returning `?:` with a recursive self-call in a
// branch, must not be misrouted into the split-BocGroup Schedule pattern.
// bodyHasBocCallsInStmtPos previously flagged the branch's self-call as a
// stmt-position boc call even though the conditional is lowered as a
// value-returning IIFE (not an IfStmt with spawns) whenever it's the last
// element and the result type isn't std.Unit -- creating an unused BocGroup
// and a WaitStmt appended after the branch's ReturnStmt. That dangling Wait
// then triggered codegen's split-BocGroup path, whose Schedule closure
// signature is hardcoded to func() std.Unit regardless of the boc's actual
// result type.
count_down #(n Int, String) {
    n <= 0 ? {
        "done"
    }, {
        count_down(n - 1)
    }
}

main: {
    print(count_down(3))
}
